# js/supabase-config.js is intentionally NOT ignored — it only holds the
# public anon key, which is safe to ship client-side (RLS policies in
# sql/schema.sql control actual access). Keeping it out of git meant it
# never reached Netlify on deploy, so the app had no Supabase connection
# in production (no spots/pins would load). If you rotate to a different
# key strategy later, re-add an ignore rule here.
